# Evaluations (Mastra scorers)

The eval system lives in `evals/` and uses **Mastra scorers** (not Confident AI / DeepEval — those were removed).

## Run

```bash
npm run eval:scorer-fixture        # fixture-only; frozen referenceOutput (not live agent quality)
npm run eval                       # documented alias of eval:scorer-fixture
npm run eval:scorer-fixture -- --samples=5
npm run eval:agent-contract        # beat-draft workflow contract tests (no live model)
npm run eval:dashboard             # open dashboard (next dev)
```

Judge: `OPENAI_API_KEY` or `JUDGING_MODEL` in `.env.local` (Mastra LLM-as-judge via `createScorer`).

`eval:scorer-fixture` is **not** agent quality. Pre-commit requires `comparison.passed === true`; a missing `passed` key is skipped, and skipped is not a pass.

## Layout

- `src/shared/agent-kernel/scorers/` — `consistency`, `hallucination`, `magic`, `persona-fidelity` (registered on Mastra)
- `evals/datasets/storyteller-golden.ts` — 12 golden examples
- `evals/run.ts` — batch runner; `evals/report/generate.ts` — HTML report; `evals/results/latest.json`
- `evals/types.ts`, `evals/tsconfig.json`

## When to run evals

- Any change to a Mastra agent prompt, tool, or model config.
- Any change to storyteller generation flow.
- Workflow contract changes: `npm run eval:agent-contract`.

## Interpreting results

Read `evals/results/latest.json`. A change is an improvement only if scores go up **without** regressing any single scorer below baseline. See `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`.
